                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- Example Pipeline Section (Interactive-like) -->
            <section class="py-20 px-8 lg:px-16 border-b border-base-content/20 bg-base-100 relative">

                <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto relative z-10">
                    <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row justify-between md:items-end mb-10">
                        <div>
                            <span class="font-mono text-xs text-accent-ink font-bold tracking-widest uppercase mb-2 block">WORKFLOW</span>
                            <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-base-content">The Selector Pipeline</h2>
                            <p class="text-base-content/88 mt-2 max-w-xl">Query, filter, mutate: how a refactor moves through the shell. A human, <code class="text-xs bg-primary/10 px-1">jq</code>, or an agent can stand at any join.</p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="hidden md:block">
                             <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-mono text-base-content/82">
                                <span class="w-3 h-3 bg-neutral rounded-full"></span> Query
                                <span class="w-3 h-3 bg-accent rounded-full ml-2"></span> Plan
                                <span class="w-3 h-3 bg-primary rounded-full ml-2"></span> Commit
                             </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    {# The end-to-end pipeline illustration is withdrawn until it is
                       regenerated for the selector pipeline: the current plate is
                       lettered OBSERVE / ACT / VERIFY, which this page now retires. #}

                    <!-- Pipeline Steps -->
                    <div class="space-y-4">

                        <!-- Step 1: Query -->
                        <div class="bg-white border border-base-content/20 p-6 rounded-xs shadow-xs relative overflow-hidden">
                            <div class="absolute left-0 top-0 bottom-0 w-1 bg-primary"></div>
                            <div class="flex flex-col lg:flex-row gap-6">
                                <div class="lg:w-1/3 flex flex-col justify-center">
                                    <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
                                        <span class="font-mono text-xs font-bold bg-primary text-base-100 px-2 py-0.5 rounded-xs">01</span>
                                        <h3 class="font-serif text-xl text-base-content">Query Symbols</h3>
                                    </div>
                                    <p class="text-sm text-base-content/88 mb-4">A structural pattern selects every matching function. Matches leave as a deterministic selector stream, closed by a completion record.</p>
                                    <div class="font-mono text-xs text-base-content/78 bg-base-100 p-2 border border-base-content/10 rounded-sm">
                                        <span class="text-accent-ink">$</span> weaver symbols list \<br>
                                        &nbsp;&nbsp;--lang rust \<br>
                                        &nbsp;&nbsp;--query 'fn $NAME($...ARGS)' --json
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                                <div tabindex="0" class="lg:w-2/3 bg-neutral p-4 rounded-xs font-mono text-xs text-code-text overflow-x-auto border border-base-content/10 shadow-inner">
<pre>
<span class="text-code-muted">// one JSONL record per match, then exactly one completion record</span>
{"schema":"weaver.selector.v1","uri":"file:///src/lib.rs","language":"rust","span":{"start":1042,"end":1187},"captures":{"NAME":{"text":"old_run"}},"source":{"digest":"sha256:9f2c..."}}
{"schema":"weaver.selector-stream-end.v1","matches":1,"complete":true}
</pre>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <!-- Connector -->
                        <div class="flex justify-center h-6">
                            <div class="w-px bg-primary/30 border-l border-dashed border-base-content"></div>
                        </div>

                        <!-- Step 2: Plan -->
                        <div class="bg-white border border-base-content/20 p-6 rounded-xs shadow-xs relative overflow-hidden">
                            <div class="absolute left-0 top-0 bottom-0 w-1 bg-accent"></div>
                            <div class="flex flex-col lg:flex-row gap-6">
                                <div class="lg:w-1/3 flex flex-col justify-center">
                                    <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
                                        <span class="font-mono text-xs font-bold bg-accent-deep text-white px-2 py-0.5 rounded-xs">02</span>
                                        <h3 class="font-serif text-xl text-base-content">Plan the Rename</h3>
                                    </div>
                                    <p class="text-sm text-base-content/88 mb-4">Selectors pipe straight into an actuator. The actuator reads the complete stream, validates the completion record, and only then plans &ndash; <code class="text-xs bg-primary/10 px-1">--dry-run</code> shows the plan without committing.</p>
                                    <div class="font-mono text-xs text-base-content/78 bg-base-100 p-2 border border-base-content/10 rounded-sm">
                                        <span class="text-accent-ink">$</span> ... | weaver symbols rename \<br>
                                        &nbsp;&nbsp;--selectors - --new-name run --dry-run
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                                <div tabindex="0" class="lg:w-2/3 bg-neutral p-4 rounded-xs font-mono text-xs text-code-text overflow-x-auto border border-base-content/10 shadow-inner">
<pre>
<span class="text-code-muted">// the plan, not the commit</span>
{"dry_run":true,"operations":3,"files":["src/lib.rs","src/main.rs","tests/run.rs"],"verification":{"syntactic":"ok","semantic":"ok"}}
</pre>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <!-- Connector -->
                        <div class="flex justify-center h-6">
                            <div class="w-px bg-primary/30 border-l border-dashed border-base-content"></div>
                        </div>

                        <!-- Step 3: Commit -->
                        <div class="bg-white border border-base-content/20 p-6 rounded-xs shadow-xs relative overflow-hidden">
                            <div class="absolute left-0 top-0 bottom-0 w-1 bg-status-ok-strong"></div>
                            <div class="flex flex-col lg:flex-row gap-6">
                                <div class="lg:w-1/3 flex flex-col justify-center">
                                    <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
                                        <span class="font-mono text-xs font-bold bg-status-ok-strong text-white px-2 py-0.5 rounded-xs">03</span>
                                        <h3 class="font-serif text-xl text-base-content">Commit, Verified</h3>
                                    </div>
                                    <p class="text-sm text-base-content/88 mb-4">Dropping <code class="text-xs bg-primary/10 px-1">--dry-run</code> commits atomically. The result carries the transaction, digests, and the diagnostics delta &ndash; and stale sources are refused, twice.</p>
                                    <div class="font-mono text-xs text-base-content/78 bg-base-100 p-2 border border-base-content/10 rounded-sm">
                                        <span class="text-accent-ink">$</span> ... | weaver symbols rename \<br>
                                        &nbsp;&nbsp;--selectors - --new-name run --json
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                                <div tabindex="0" class="lg:w-2/3 bg-neutral p-4 rounded-xs font-mono text-xs text-code-text overflow-x-auto border border-base-content/10 shadow-inner">
<pre>
<span class="text-code-muted">// transaction result with the diagnostics delta</span>
{"transaction":"txn_01j9...","changed":["src/lib.rs","src/main.rs","tests/run.rs"],"diagnostics":{"introduced":0,"resolved":0,"unchanged":12}}
</pre>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                    </div>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- Common Flags & Exit Codes -->
            <section class="py-16 px-8 lg:px-16 border-b border-base-content/20 bg-white/40">
                <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-12">

                    <!-- Common Flags -->
                    <div>
                        <h3 class="font-serif text-2xl text-base-content mb-6">Global Flags</h3>
                        <div class="reference-callout mb-6">
                            <div class="reference-callout-title">
                                {{ icon('book-open') }}
                                Canonical reference
                            </div>
                            <p class="text-sm text-base-content/80 mb-3">
                                Keep command semantics on this page. Keep config defaults, override precedence, and the wire protocol in the docs hub.
                            </p>
                            <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 text-xs font-mono">
                                <a href="/weaver/docs/#configuration" class="text-accent-ink hover:underline">Configuration</a>
                                <a href="/weaver/docs/#jsonl-schema" class="text-accent-ink hover:underline">JSONL protocol</a>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="bg-base-100 border border-base-content/20 rounded-xs overflow-hidden">
                            <table class="w-full text-left">
                                <tbody class="divide-y divide-base-content/10">
                                    <tr>
                                        <td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs text-accent-ink bg-primary/5 w-44">--json</td>
                                        <td class="p-3 text-sm text-base-content/80">The one machine switch. Emits the stable JSON contract for the command; without it, the localized human renderer applies.</td>
                                    </tr>
                                    <tr>
                                        <td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs text-accent-ink bg-primary/5">--plain / --color / --width / --no-pager / --locale</td>
                                        <td class="p-3 text-sm text-base-content/80">Human-renderer controls. Colour never carries meaning alone; ASCII and narrow-width fallbacks are first-class.</td>
                                    </tr>
                                    <tr>
                                        <td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs text-accent-ink bg-primary/5">--profile</td>
                                        <td class="p-3 text-sm text-base-content/80">Select a saved profile. Precedence: built-in defaults &lt; config files &lt; profile &lt; environment &lt; flags. Secrets are redacted on output.</td>
                                    </tr>
                                    <tr>
                                        <td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs text-accent-ink bg-primary/5">--config-path</td>
                                        <td class="p-3 text-sm text-base-content/80">Path to an explicit <code class="text-xs bg-primary/10 px-1">weaver.toml</code> configuration file.</td>
                                    </tr>
                                    <tr>
                                        <td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs text-accent-ink bg-primary/5">--daemon-socket</td>
                                        <td class="p-3 text-sm text-base-content/80">Override daemon transport (e.g. <code class="text-xs bg-primary/10 px-1">unix:///run/user/1000/weaver.sock</code>).</td>
                                    </tr>
                                    <tr>
                                        <td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs text-accent-ink bg-primary/5">--dry-run / --force</td>
                                        <td class="p-3 text-sm text-base-content/80">Standard mutation safety flags. <code class="text-xs bg-primary/10 px-1">--force</code> never overrides a stale-source refusal; an override must name the newly accepted source version.</td>
                                    </tr>
                                </tbody>
                            </table>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Exit Codes -->
                    <div>
                        <h3 class="font-serif text-2xl text-base-content mb-6">Exit Codes &amp; Errors</h3>
                        <div class="bg-base-100 border border-base-content/20 rounded-xs overflow-hidden mb-6">
                            <table class="w-full text-left">
                                <tbody class="divide-y divide-base-content/10">
                                    <tr>
                                        <td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs font-bold text-base-content bg-primary/5 w-16 text-center">0</td>
                                        <td class="p-3 text-sm text-base-content/80">Success &ndash; including a query with zero matches, which still emits its completion record.</td>
                                    </tr>
                                    <tr>
                                        <td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs font-bold text-base-content bg-primary/5 text-center">1</td>
                                        <td class="p-3 text-sm text-base-content/80">General error (file not found, permission denied).</td>
                                    </tr>
                                    <tr>
                                        <td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs font-bold text-base-content bg-primary/5 text-center">126</td>
                                        <td class="p-3 text-sm text-base-content/80">Command invoked cannot execute (sandbox restriction).</td>
                                    </tr>
                                    <tr>
                                        <td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs font-bold text-base-content bg-primary/5 text-center">130</td>
                                        <td class="p-3 text-sm text-base-content/80">Terminated by signal (Ctrl-C).</td>
                                    </tr>
                                </tbody>
                            </table>
                        </div>
                        <p class="text-sm text-base-content/80">
                            Errors teach. Every enum-shaped rejection names the invalid value, the valid values and their source registry, a stable error code, an exit class, and a working next command. Guessing is not part of the contract.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- Introspection & Output Contract -->
            <section id="discovery" class="py-16 px-8 lg:px-16 border-b border-base-content/20">
                <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto">
                    <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-base-content mb-8">Introspection &amp; Output</h2>
                    <div class="reference-callout mb-8">
                        <div class="reference-callout-title">
                            {{ icon('book-open') }}
                            Canonical reference
                        </div>
                        <p class="text-sm text-base-content/80 mb-3">
                            This page keeps the command map. The authoritative defaults, override syntax, and wire envelope live in the docs hub so those details only drift in one place.
                        </p>
                        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 text-xs font-mono">
                            <a href="/weaver/docs/#configuration" class="text-accent-ink hover:underline">Configuration</a>
                            <a href="/weaver/docs/#jsonl-schema" class="text-accent-ink hover:underline">JSONL protocol</a>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
                        <div class="bg-white border border-base-content/15 p-6 rounded-xs">
                            <h3 class="font-mono text-xs font-bold text-base-content uppercase tracking-wider mb-3">The contract, as data</h3>
                            <p class="text-sm text-base-content/75 leading-relaxed">
                                <code>weaver context --json</code> emits the whole surface: schema version, commands, flags, enum values, output schemas, error taxonomy, and capabilities. Agents read it once and stop guessing.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="bg-white border border-base-content/15 p-6 rounded-xs">
                            <h3 class="font-mono text-xs font-bold text-base-content uppercase tracking-wider mb-3">Capability probe</h3>
                            <p class="text-sm text-base-content/75 leading-relaxed">
                                <code>weaver capabilities list --json</code> reports runtime availability with a deterministic provider-selection rationale. Providers stay behind capabilities; their names surface only in provenance and verbose output.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="bg-white border border-base-content/15 p-6 rounded-xs">
                            <h3 class="font-mono text-xs font-bold text-base-content uppercase tracking-wider mb-3">Non-interactive by default</h3>
                            <p class="text-sm text-base-content/75 leading-relaxed">
                                No implicit prompts. Interaction happens only under <code>--interactive</code> or a dedicated review command, and a non-TTY stdin fails fast with a structured error.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- CLI Help Discoverability (PLANNED) -->
            <section class="py-16 px-8 lg:px-16 border-b border-base-content/20 bg-white/40">
                <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto">
                    <div class="border-2 border-dashed border-base-content/40 rounded-xs p-8 opacity-80">
                        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-6">
                            <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-base-content">CLI Help &amp; Discoverability</h2>
                            <span class="status-pill status-pill-planned">Planned</span>
                        </div>

                        <p class="mb-6 text-sm text-base-content/80">
                            Help text, manpages, and shell completions all generate from the single command contract behind <code class="text-xs bg-primary/10 px-1">context --json</code>, with drift gates in CI. One source; no stale runbooks.
                        </p>

                        <div class="border border-base-content/20 rounded-xs bg-white overflow-hidden mb-6">
                            <table class="w-full text-left text-sm">
                                <thead class="bg-primary/80 text-white font-mono text-xs uppercase">
                                    <tr>
                                        <th class="p-4 font-medium">Command</th>
                                        <th class="p-4 font-medium">Behaviour</th>
                                    </tr>
                                </thead>
                                <tbody class="divide-y divide-base-content/10">
                                    <tr class="hover:bg-base-100/30">
                                        <td class="p-4 font-mono text-base-content font-bold text-xs">weaver --help</td>
                                        <td class="p-4 text-base-content/80">Lists every resource and its verbs, plus global options and a quick-start example. Does not require a running daemon.</td>
                                    </tr>
                                    <tr class="hover:bg-base-100/30">
                                        <td class="p-4 font-mono text-base-content font-bold text-xs">weaver &lt;resource&gt;</td>
                                        <td class="p-4 text-base-content/80">Without a verb, prints the verbs available for that resource and a follow-up <code class="text-xs bg-primary/10 px-1">--help</code> hint.</td>
                                    </tr>
                                    <tr class="hover:bg-base-100/30">
                                        <td class="p-4 font-mono text-base-content font-bold text-xs">weaver &lt;resource&gt; &lt;verb&gt; --help</td>
                                        <td class="p-4 text-base-content/80">Command-level help with required arguments, examples, and exit codes.</td>
                                    </tr>
                                    <tr class="hover:bg-base-100/30">
                                        <td class="p-4 font-mono text-base-content font-bold text-xs">weaver skill-path</td>
                                        <td class="p-4 text-base-content/80">Prints the paths to agent-facing skill documents shipped with the binary.</td>
                                    </tr>
                                </tbody>
                            </table>
                        </div>

                        <h3 class="font-serif text-lg text-base-content mb-3">Actionable Errors</h3>
                        <p class="text-sm text-base-content/80">
                            An invalid resource lists all valid resources. An unknown verb suggests the nearest match. Every error path follows the same three-part template: problem statement, valid alternatives, and an explicit next command.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </section>

